---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import { helloEmail } from "../../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="LoopLogic Terms of Service — scubadeving"
  description="Terms of service for LoopLogic, a CCR dive operations and analytics app by scubadeving."
  ogImage="/og-looplogic.png"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">

    <Header showBack={true} />

    <main>
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
          LoopLogic Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated: August 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-400/20 bg-amber-400/5 px-4 py-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-amber-400">
          This document is a working draft. It has not been reviewed by legal counsel.
          Do not rely on it as a final legal instrument — have it reviewed by a qualified
          attorney before public release.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="mb-24 space-y-12">

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            1. Agreement to terms
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            By downloading, installing, or using LoopLogic ("the App"), you agree to be bound
            by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, do not
            use the App. These Terms apply to all users of the App, including beta testers
            and early-access participants.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            2. Description of service
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            LoopLogic is a closed-circuit rebreather (CCR) operations and analytics app that
            provides pre-dive checklists, O₂ cell health tracking, scrubber usage logging,
            and related record-keeping functionality. The App operates entirely offline and
            stores all data locally on your device.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            3. Safety and life support disclaimer
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">
              Read this section carefully. It directly affects your safety.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              LoopLogic is a <strong class="font-medium text-ink">supplemental record-keeping
              and planning tool only</strong>. It is not a dive computer, not a life support
              instrument, and must never be used as the primary or sole basis for any
              safety-critical decision during a dive.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              Diving with a closed-circuit rebreather involves inherent risks that can result
              in serious injury or death. You are solely responsible for:
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted list-disc">
              <li>Cross-verifying all checklist results, cell readings, and scrubber data against manufacturer-approved instruments and procedures.</li>
              <li>Making all go/no-go dive decisions based on your own training, experience, and manufacturer-approved equipment.</li>
              <li>Ensuring your rebreather is in a safe, serviceable condition before every dive.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              scubadeving makes no representation that the App's data, readings, or
              recommendations are accurate, complete, or suitable for any particular dive.
              The App may contain bugs, calculation errors, or inaccuracies. Never substitute
              the App for proper dive training, equipment maintenance, or manufacturer guidance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            4. Beta software notice
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            LoopLogic is currently pre-release software. Beta and early-access versions may
            contain bugs, incomplete features, or unexpected behavior. By participating in
            beta testing you acknowledge that:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 ml-4 space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted list-disc">
            <li>The App is not production-ready and should be used with additional caution.</li>
            <li>Data stored in beta versions may not migrate to future releases.</li>
            <li>Access to the beta may be modified or revoked at any time.</li>
            <li>Feedback you provide may be used to improve the App without compensation.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            5. Permitted use
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            You may use the App for personal, non-commercial dive record-keeping and planning.
            You may not: reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the App; redistribute
            or resell the App or its content; use the App in any way that violates applicable
            law; or misrepresent the App's output as certified dive equipment data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            6. Intellectual property
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The App, including its design, code, and content, is the property of scubadeving
            and is protected by applicable intellectual property law. These Terms do not
            grant you any ownership rights in the App. Open-source components used in the
            App are governed by their respective licenses, which are disclosed within the App.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            7. Disclaimer of warranties
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The App is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind,
            express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
            fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement. scubadeving does
            not warrant that the App will be error-free, uninterrupted, or free of harmful
            components.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            8. Limitation of liability
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, scubadeving shall not be liable for any
            indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from
            your use of or inability to use the App — including but not limited to personal
            injury, death, loss of data, or equipment damage — regardless of the theory of
            liability and even if scubadeving has been advised of the possibility of such damages.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            scubadeving's total liability to you for any claim arising from these Terms or
            your use of the App shall not exceed the amount you paid for the App in the
            twelve months preceding the claim.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            9. Governing law
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, United States,
            without regard to conflict of law principles. Any disputes arising under these
            Terms shall be resolved in the state or federal courts located in California.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            10. Changes to these terms
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            scubadeving reserves the right to update these Terms at any time. Updated Terms
            will be posted at this URL with a revised date. Continued use of the App after
            changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            11. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Questions about these Terms may be directed to{" "}
            <a
              href={`mailto:${helloEmail}`}
              class="rounded underline text-accent transition-colors focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
            >
              {helloEmail}
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />

  </div>
</Layout>
